Title: 0003-aros-absolute-paths
Repository: pragtical
Base-Commit: 5c05f09e081833b581fb5ecd10e64963dec87f03
Requires: 0002-aros-stack-exepath-realpath.patch
Author: aros-pragtical project
Date: 2026-09-20
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: AROS system.absolute_path, system.chdir, and common.is_absolute_path.

Problem:
  posixc realpath('.') returns NULL on a volume:path cwd, so core.set_project never ran and load_plugins indexed a nil root_project. Unix is_absolute_path also treated Qemu Vvfat:Pragtical as relative.
Solution:
  Resolve '.' via SDL_GetCurrentDirectory, keep volume:path as already-absolute, join relative names onto that cwd; treat a colon before any slash as an AROS absolute path; strip a non-root trailing slash before chdir.
Validation:
  The Pragtical 3.14.0 x86_64 ABIv1 build compiled and linked, all 15 focused Lua cases passed, and runtime checks covered nested and volume-root opening, saving and command-line reopening on 2026-11-15.
Removal:
  Remove only when the pinned upstream contains equivalent AROS path handling and both x86_64 targets pass their regressions.

diff --git a/data/core/common.lua b/data/core/common.lua
index 5c6edd0f..555aef70 100644
--- a/data/core/common.lua
+++ b/data/core/common.lua
@@ -784,6 +784,12 @@ end
 ---@param path string
 ---@return boolean
 function common.is_absolute_path(path)
+  if PLATFORM == "AROS" then
+    -- Volume:path is absolute; a colon after a slash is a name, not a device.
+    local colon = path:find(":", 1, true)
+    local slash = path:find("/", 1, true)
+    return colon ~= nil and (slash == nil or colon < slash)
+  end
   return path:sub(1, 1) == PATHSEP or path:match("^(%a):\\")
 end
 
